        "y0": 0.4351856060606061,
        "x1": 0.480936274509804,
        "y1": 0.5063131313131313
      },
      "text": "where D = 0 . 01 is the diffusion coefficient and K = 0 . 01 is the reaction rate. Here, we use u ( x,t ) = ( πx ) / 5 + u 1 ( t ) , where u 1 ( t ) is a sampling function from the GRF. In addition, we consider the KS equation, which exhibits complex chaotic dynamics, of the following form",
      "html": null,
